From b97f6ae5c3bad1bceeef30787191a5edac87d4c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 06:13:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sandbox): docker skills mount is always the
 live-refreshed sanitized copy

A clean skills dir was bind-mounted raw at container creation, so a skills/.hub
(later hub install) or a skill .env created afterwards appeared at once in the
live read-only mount of a long-lived or reused container; a dirty dir that
later became clean left the container on a stale copy.

- get_skills_directory_mount always mounts the sanitized copy (option (a) of
  the review): the copy only ever receives files the read guard allows.
- Copies live at a stable per-source path, <HERMES_HOME>/cache/sandbox-skills/
  <sha16(realpath)>, not a per-process mkdtemp deleted at exit (that emptied
  the mount of any container a later process reused). Refreshes are serialized
  across threads and processes (skill_file_lock).
- DockerEnvironment._before_execute refreshes the copies in place at most every
  5 s (the FileSyncManager tick); a refresh failure is logged, never fails the
  command. Capsule envs (no skills mounts) never refresh.
- The walk prunes the copy store, so a skills root containing HERMES_HOME
  never copies the copies into themselves (mount and sync views stay equal).
- _refresh_sanitized_copy keys on path strings: warm no-op refresh of a
  5,000-file tree went 254 ms -> 125 ms (cold copy 0.36 s), on par with the
  existing remote sync tick walk (iter_skills_files, 106 ms).

Containers created before this change mounted the raw dir, so their reuse
fingerprint differs and the first session after upgrade starts a fresh one.

Proof: tests/tools/test_docker_skills_mount_live.py (new; 5/5 red on 62c90b6d51,
green here): after start, skills/.hub/x and skills/s/.env never appear in the
mounted source, a new skills/s/SKILL.md does after the next refresh point;
dirty->clean converges. test_credential_files, test_docker_environment,
test_file_sync + 9 neighbouring files: 277 passed. scripts/check: ok.
